To calculate $\binom{19}{9}$, we start by applying Pascal's identity, which tells us that for any integers $n$ and $k$, $\binom{n}{k}=\binom{n-1}{k-1}+\binom{n-1}{k}$. Using this, we can express $\binom{19}{9}$ as follows:

\[
\binom{19}{9} = \binom{18}{8} + \binom{18}{9}
\]

We can then apply Pascal's identity again to both terms on the right-hand side:

\[
\begin{align*}
\binom{19}{9} &= \left(\binom{17}{7} + \binom{17}{8}\right) + \left(\binom{17}{8} + \binom{17}{9}\right) \\
&= \binom{17}{7} + 2\cdot\binom{17}{8} + \binom{17}{9}
\end{align*}
\]

Substituting the given values for $\binom{17}{7}=19448$, $\binom{17}{8}=24310$, and $\binom{17}{9}=24310$, we get:

\[
\begin{align*}
\binom{19}{9} &= 19448 + 2\cdot24310 + 24310 \\
&= 19448 + 48620 + 24310 \\
&= 92378
\end{align*}
\]

Therefore, $\binom{19}{9} = \boxed{92378}$.

